From: hashtagbasit
Subject: media: iris: stop Steam Remote Play staying green

After the first source change Steam stops and restarts the bitstream
port, and the driver hands the firmware its stream settings again. Two of
them never matched what the firmware had reported, so it raised the same
source change on every restart and returned no picture (a green screen):

- the picture order count type went back as 0 instead of the stream's
  type, so most H.264 streams mismatched;
- TIER_AV1's setter runs for every codec and wrote 0 over the HEVC tier
  that iris_hfi_gen2_set_tier() had just set, so High tier HEVC
  mismatched. set_tier() already picks the AV1 tier for AV1, so the setter
  goes.

diff -ru a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c
@@ -179,7 +179,6 @@
 		.value = 0,
 		.hfi_id = HFI_PROP_TIER,
 		.flags = CAP_FLAG_INPUT_PORT,
-		.set = iris_set_u32,
 	},
 	{
 		.cap_id = DRAP,
diff -ru a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
@@ -339,7 +339,7 @@
 {
 	struct iris_inst_hfi_gen2 *inst_hfi_gen2 = to_iris_inst_hfi_gen2(inst);
 	u32 port = iris_hfi_gen2_get_port(inst, plane);
-	u32 poc = 0;
+	u32 poc = inst->fw_caps[POC].value;
 
 	inst_hfi_gen2->src_subcr_params.pic_order_cnt = poc;
 
